<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by an assertion failure in `ada::helpers::substring`, which is called by `ada::url_aggregator::get_hash`. The assertion `pos <= input.size()` fails because `get_hash` passes a `pos` value (119) that is larger than the size of the input string (81). This indicates an incorrect calculation or state management within the `ada::url_aggregator`'s `get_hash` method when handling a malformed or specific URL provided by the fuzzer.

The fuzz driver is behaving correctly by calling the public API of the `ada` library. The bug is in the project's implementation of `get_hash`.

Suggestion for the project:
The developers of the `ada` library should review the implementation of `ada::url_aggregator::get_hash` to ensure that it correctly handles all possible URL states, including invalid or unusual ones. The calculation of the starting position for the hash component needs to be validated against the actual length of the URL's internal string representation before calling `substring`. A check should be added to prevent out-of-bounds access.
</crash-analysis>

